<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Arch on A Moment's Rest</title><link>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/tags/arch/</link><description>Recent content in Arch on A Moment's Rest</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:53:16 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.a-moment.top/en/tags/arch/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Installing Arch Linux on a Laptop (Physical Machine)</title><link>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/others/arch_on_laptop/</link><pubDate>Fri, 02 May 2025 16:12:04 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/others/arch_on_laptop/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://blog.a-moment.top/images/Alice.png" alt="Featured image of post Installing Arch Linux on a Laptop (Physical Machine)" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Installing Arch Linux on a virtual machine before was just not satisfying enough (lol, you didn&amp;rsquo;t even finish the series (x)), so this time I&amp;rsquo;m putting Arch on my little thin-and-light. And along the way, documenting the pitfalls you might hit on real hardware?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The header image is from R Sound Design&amp;rsquo;s new track 《アリス？》, a really cheerful Vocaloid song~ Bilibili &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1UtV5zqEjC/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;submission&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/aplayer/dist/APlayer.min.css"&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer {&#13;&#10; background: var(--card-background);&#13;&#10; border: 1px solid var(--card-separator-color);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer.aplayer-withlist .aplayer-info {&#13;&#10; border-bottom-color: var(--card-separator-color);&#13